.SH "struct pdg::SpriteBreakEvent"
.PP 
\fBSpriteBreakEvent\fP\&. 

A body exceeded its angular-speed threshold or a legacy joint exceeded its break force\&.

.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
Documentation-only JavaScript shape, not a runtime constructor\&.
.RE
.PP
 
.PP
\fBFields\fP
.RS 4
Field  Type  Required/default  Meaning  actingSprite  \fR\fBSprite\fP\fP or \fRnull\fP  Required  action  \fRnumber\fP  Required  angularSpeed  \fRnumber\fP  Required  body  \fR\fBPhysicsBody\fP\fP or \fRnull\fP  Required  breakAngularSpeed  \fRnumber\fP  Required  breakForce  \fRnumber\fP  Required  emitter  \fR\fBEventEmitter\fP\fP  Required  eventType  \fRnumber\fP  Required  force  \fRnumber\fP  Required  impulse  \fRnumber\fP  Required  inLayer  \fR\fBSpriteLayer\fP\fP or \fRnull\fP  Required  joint  \fR\fBCpConstraint\fP\fP or \fRnull\fP  Required  part  \fR\fBPart\fP\fP or \fRnull\fP  Required  reason  \fRnumber\fP  Required  referenceBody  \fR\fBPhysicsBody\fP\fP or \fRnull\fP  Required  targetSprite  \fR\fBSprite\fP\fP or \fRnull\fP  Required  
.RE
.PP
Register an \fBIEventHandler\fP for eventType_SpriteBreak on the owning \fBSprite\fP\&. \fBPart\fP body notifications use their owning \fBSprite\fP's route\&. Inspect reason to distinguish the two event forms\&. Body notifications work with both basic and Chipmunk solvers\&.

.PP
 
.PP
\fBBreak event fields\fP
.RS 4

.RE
.PP
Field  Meaning  emitter, eventType  Standard event emitter and eventType_SpriteBreak\&.  actingSprite, inLayer  Owning \fBSprite\fP and its layer (null outside a layer)\&.  reason  physicsBreak_AngularSpeed or physicsBreak_Force\&.  action  action_BodyBreak for speed; action_JointBreak for legacy force breaks\&.  body, part  Source \fBPhysicsBody\fP and optional \fBPart\fP for speed; null for legacy force breaks\&.  referenceBody  Optional angular-speed reference \fBPhysicsBody\fP, otherwise null\&.  angularSpeed  Measured speed magnitude in radians/second; zero for force breaks\&.  breakAngularSpeed  Configured speed threshold in radians/second; zero for force breaks\&.  targetSprite, joint  Legacy joint endpoint and \fBCpConstraint\fP; null for speed events\&.  impulse, force, breakForce  Legacy joint impulse, solved force and break threshold; zero for speed events\&.  

.PP

.PP
Angular-speed notifications do not clamp speed, apply braking, disconnect joints or split artwork, regardless of the handler's return value\&. They fire once per sampled excursion above the limit; returning to or below the limit rearms them\&. See \fBPhysicsBody\&.setBreakAngularSpeed()\fP for sampling and reference lifetime rules\&.

.PP
Legacy Chipmunk joint-force events retain their existing behavior: returning true handles the notification; an unhandled event invokes the existing disconnect path\&. Shared \fBPhysicsConstraint\fP force breaking retains its existing behavior too; this body feature does not add force events to that separate constraint path\&.

.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBPhysicsBody\&.setBreakAngularSpeed()\fP, \fBpdg\&.eventType_SpriteBreak\fP 
.RE
.PP

