Field  Type  Required/default  Meaning  alt  \fRboolean\fP  Required  buttonNumber  \fRnumber\fP  Required  ctrl  \fRboolean\fP  Required  emitter  \fR\fBEventEmitter\fP\fP  Required  eventType  \fRnumber\fP  Required  inLayer  \fR\fBSpriteLayer\fP\fP  Required  lastClickElapsed  \fRnumber\fP  Required  lastClickPos  \fR\fBPoint\fP\fP  Required  leftButton  \fRboolean\fP  Required  meta  \fRboolean\fP  Required  mousePos  \fR\fBPoint\fP\fP  Required  rightButton  \fRboolean\fP  Required  shift  \fRboolean\fP  Required  touchedSprite  \fR\fBSprite\fP\fP  Required  touchType  \fRnumber\fP  Required  
.RE
.PP
This event is generated by a \fBSprite\fP whenever a user clicks on it (or touches it in on a touch device)\&.

.PP
.PP
.nf
{
    emitter: {},            // the emitter that generated this event
    eventType: 19,          // the event type (eventType_SpriteTouch)
    shift: false,           // true if the shift key is held down
    ctrl: false,            // true if the control key is held down
    alt: false,             // true if the alt (or option) key is held down
    meta: false,            // true if the meta (windows or command) key is held down
    mousePos: {
        x: 456,             // the x coordinate of the mouse when the event occurred
        y: 201              // the y coordinate of the mouse when the event occurred
    },
    leftButton: false,      // true if the left mouse button was down
    rightButton: false,     // true if the right mouse button was down
    buttonNumber: 0,        // button number (0=left, 1=right, 2=middle) or finger ID for touch
    lastClickPos: { 
        x: 456,             // the x coordinate of the last mouseDown event
        y: 201              // the y coordinate of the last mouseDown event
    },
    lastClickElapsed: 201,  // the number of milliseconds since the last mouseDown
    touchType: 22,          // touch_MouseDown(22), touch_MouseUp(23), or touch_MouseClick(24)
    touchedSprite: {},      // the Sprite that was clicked or touched
    inLayer: {}             // the SpriteLayer that contains the Sprite
}  
.fi
.PP

.PP
A single click may generate up to three separate events, each with a different touchType:

.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBpdg\&.touch_MouseDown\fP when a mouse button goes down inside a \fBSprite\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBpdg\&.touch_MouseUp\fP when a mouse button is released inside a \fBSprite\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBpdg\&.touch_MouseClick\fP when the mouse button was clicked and released inside the same \fBSprite\fP
.PP

.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
Click events must be turned on for each \fBSprite\fP using \fBSprite\&.setWantsClickEvents()\fP

.PP
If no \fBSprite\fP was hit by a mouse event, the original \fBpdg\&.eventType_MouseDown\fP or \fBpdg\&.eventType_MouseUp\fP is passed on through the \fBEventManager\fP
.RE
.PP

.PP
\fBSee also\fP
